###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I also lists CUR (16, 32), CUR k=1, FPS and PC selections with 16, 32 and 64 SFs per element, and Table II CUR with 16 and 32 SFs per species; only the 64-SF CUR models and the published reference sets are encoded as runs.
# - Vacancy-migration barriers of Al, Mg and Si (Fig. 2; error 'below 0.1 eV') are property comparisons and are not encoded.
# - QM7b atomization-energy GPR with CUR/FPS-reduced SOAP features (Figs. 3-4) is not an interatomic potential; its errors are only in figures.
# - The DFT functional for either reference data set is not restated in this paper. The atom count 648 is 216 x 3 atoms for the 216-molecule water box.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/imbalzano2018.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

